#
# Conformance case: teleology/choice-combinator.
#
# A logic:Choice is EXECUTED under executional entailment: its logic:guardSituation (requestPresent) holds at the start state, so control dispatches to the LEFT operand (serveRequest), which runs and asserts requestServed. The engine records a logic:TransactionOutcome (logic:transactionSucceeds true) with the executed path. The dual guard-false dispatch is the choice-guard-false case. Proves guard-true dispatch — a PROGRAM operator, not a conditional formula connective.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom the
# projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live in
# input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/choice-combinator/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
